/new/ARC_code/train/3ad05f52.py:132:    - The grid has a dominant background, one wall color forming thin orthogonal frames, and one endpoint/fill color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/arc_utils.py:67:        (0x7F, 0xDB, 0xFF),  # 8 teal/azure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/db7260a4.py:62:    assert len(foreground_colors) == 2, \"expected marker and wall colors\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/18/code.py:22:#    - Original task: one wall color splits the grid into regions. Inside each region,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/18/code.py:29:#      wall color underneath that dot decides whether the palette is traversed forward\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/18/code.py:33:#      green. If that dotted wall segment uses the majority wall color, the fill order\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/18/code.py:34:#      is [green, red, green, ...]. If the same dot sat on the minority wall color,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/18/code.py:45:#      than the other. The more common wall color means \"forward\"; the less common wall\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/18/code.py:50:#      the minority wall color must have palette length >= 3 so the reverse rule changes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/18/code.py:60:#      clue dot changes the start and the wall color changes the traversal direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/18/code.py:62:#      whose same-axis neighbors keep the underlying wall color visible. The generator\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/18/code.py:63:#      enforces this so the solver can recover the hidden wall color under the clue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/18/code.py:76:#    - Across samples, regions whose dot sits on the dominant wall color progress inward\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/18/code.py:77:#      in one cyclic order, while regions whose dot sits on the rarer wall color use the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/18/code.py:90:#      wall-color frequency: more-common wall color => forward; less-common => reverse.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/18/code.py:103:#    - The wall-dot cell reveals its hidden wall color via same-axis wall neighbors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/18/code.py:105:#      aligned neighbors share the same base wall color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/18/code.py:356:    Fill walled regions with cyclic bands, using wall dots for the first color and wall colors for the traversal direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/18/code.py:359:    - Thin axis-aligned separator walls divide the board into rectangular regions, but the walls now use two dominant colors instead of one.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/18/code.py:365:    - The wall dot tells which palette color should appear on the boundary band of that region, and the underlying wall color at that dotted cell tells whether to step forward or backward through the palette as depth increases.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/18/code.py:366:    - The more common wall color means forward traversal, the less common wall color means reverse traversal; all wall pixels, including clue dots, stay unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/25/code.py:33:#     across regions via the visible corner seed geometry instead of hidden metadata.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/25/code.py:314:    - The wall color partitions the board into rectangular free regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/25/code.py:315:    - In an active region, one corner contains a 2-cell same-color seed on the first step of a hidden spiral.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/25/code.py:319:    - For each region, find the unique corner and turn direction whose spiral starts with the visible 2-cell seed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/8/code.py:324:    - One wall color partitions the canvas into several 4-connected non-wall regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/8/code.py:330:    - After all regions are painted, recolor each wall pixel with the outermost frame color of the nearest region, making the wall color disappear.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/24/code.py:222:    - One wall color splits the canvas into several 4-connected regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/1/code.py:333:    - The wall color splits the grid into rectangular free regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/3/code.py:267:    - One wall color partitions the grid into several 4-connected rooms.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/3/code.py:661:        \"tri_seed_blocker_regions\": int(tri_seed_blocker_regions),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/11/code.py:318:    - One wall color partitions the canvas into rectangular non-wall regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/47/code.py:40:     frame-wall color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/47/code.py:83:- The recolor stage assumes the final paint color is the frame-wall color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/47/code.py:100:  multi-colored input pieces vanish into the wall color in the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/47/code.py:103:  2. recolor matched content to the wall color,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/47/code.py:332:      of that piece to the frame-wall color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/47/code.py:338:    own color and merges into the wall color of the enlarged frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/7/code.py:168:    - One wall color partitions the canvas into rectangular free regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/17/code.py:23:#      - The visible objects stay the same as in the source task: one wall color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/17/code.py:73:#      - Solver assumes a wall color can still be recovered as the second-most\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/17/code.py:194:    - A single wall color partitions the board into several non-wall regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/15/code.py:22:#    - Original task: a wall color splits the board into free regions, marker\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/15/code.py:69:#    - Solver assumes the wall color is the second most common color and that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/15/code.py:246:    - One wall color partitions the grid into disjoint free regions, and every\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/20/code.py:264:    - A wall color splits the canvas into 4-connected non-wall regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/2/code.py:297:    - The wall color partitions the grid into rectangular non-wall regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/16/code.py:177:    - One wall color forms nested 1px rectangular frames, with the outermost frame on the grid border.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/9/code.py:226:    - One wall color forms several 1px closed rectangular frames nested inside each other, with non-wall regions appearing as rectangular rings plus a center chamber.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/10/code.py:226:    - One wall color partitions the grid into several 4-connected non-wall regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/42/code.py:244:    - The largest 4-connected foreground component is a rectangular frame whose base wall color is dominant.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/42/code.py:249:    - Recover the inner layout by cropping the non-wall colored regions inside the frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/21/code.py:21:#    The seed task uses one straight wall color to carve the canvas into mostly\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/21/code.py:77:#    visible boundary depth, wall color is identified structurally as the big\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/4/code.py:265:    - The grid is divided into free-space regions by one wall color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/5/code.py:208:    - A wall color partitions the grid into several non-wall regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/13/code.py:62:#    by a single wall color, and outputs contain only base-colored gaps plus a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/13/code.py:137:    - One wall color partitions the canvas into separate non-wall regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/22/code.py:147:    - The grid is split by one wall color into several 4-connected non-wall regions.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
